@@ -8,6 +8,21 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema
+  `inputSchema` before calling the executor (`required`, declared property types, and `enum`,
+  with undeclared extra properties passed through unchanged and no type coercion or default
+  injection). Static schemas are compiled synchronously at `register` time so an invalid or
+  async schema throws immediately naming the tool; function-valued tool definitions compile and
+  cache validators per schema object. When input fails validation, `execute` returns a
+  `ToolResponse` naming the failing field paths and constraints — never echoing or logging
+  offending values — instead of invoking the executor or throwing, so the model can correct the
+  call within `maxToolRounds` (`Unknown tool: <name>` still throws). Migration note: executors
+  that previously hand-validated `input` now receive only payloads their `inputSchema` already
+  accepts, and tools that relied on seeing malformed input to produce their own error message
+  stop seeing it.
+
